  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Anil Kumar vs State Of U.P. And Another on 5 May, 2023 Author: Rajiv Gupta Bench: Rajiv Gupta High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 65 Case :- Application U/S 482 No. - 16408 of 2023 Applicant :- Anil Kumar",
    "facts": "By means of present application, the applicant has challenged the bailable warrant dated 12.11.2013 as well as further proceeding of Complaint Case no. 1128 of 2013, under section 26/59 and 63 of Food Safety Act and Standard Act, pending in the court of Addl. Chief Judicial Magistrate-I, Bulandshahr. At the very outset, learned AGA for the State has submitted that the bailable warrant has been issued by the court below vide order dated 12.11.2013, however, the instant application has been filed after an expiry of more than nine and half years, as such, the present application is hopelessly barred by laches. It is further submitted that the said laches has not been explained at all, in the absence of which, the present application do not deserve any indulgence by this Court.",
    "arguments": "1 Learned counsel for the applicant has not been able to give any reasonable explanation for the said laches.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "1 Learned counsel for the applicant has not been able to give any reasonable explanation for the said laches.",
